---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import site from '../../site.config.json' with { type: 'json' };

const page = {
  url: '/corrections/', title: 'Corrections Policy',
  seoTitle: 'Corrections Policy | Marine Diesel Engine', pageType: 'policy',
  status: 'ready', author: site.defaultAuthor, reviewer: null,
  needsReviewer: false, parent: '/', parentTitle: 'Home',
  schema: ['WebPage', 'BreadcrumbList'], updated: site.legalUpdated,
  indexable: true, blockers: [], faqs: [],
  headings: [
    { depth: 2, slug: 'report-an-error', text: 'Report an error' },
    { depth: 2, slug: 'what-happens-next', text: 'What happens next' },
    { depth: 2, slug: 'business-listings', text: 'Business listings' },
  ],
  description: 'How to report factual errors, outdated marine diesel information or business-listing changes and how Marine Diesel Engine Australia handles corrections.',
  primaryKeyword: 'Marine Diesel Engine corrections policy', searchIntent: 'Navigational',
};
---
<Page page={page}>
  <h1>Corrections policy</h1>
  <p>
    We want factual errors, outdated specifications and misleading wording to be
    corrected promptly. A correction request does not need to be formal, but
    enough detail to locate and verify the issue helps us act faster.
  </p>

  <h2 id="report-an-error">Report an error</h2>
  <p>
    Use the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a> and include the page address,
    the wording or data in question, why it appears wrong and the best available
    evidence. For model-specific claims, a current manufacturer manual,
    technical bulletin or regulator publication is more useful than a forum or
    an unattributed summary.
  </p>

  <h2 id="what-happens-next">What happens next</h2>
  <p>
    We compare the report with the page's sources and any current primary
    material. Clear errors are corrected; claims that cannot yet be verified may
    be qualified, removed or held from indexing. A substantial change should
    update the page date. Minor spelling, formatting and broken-link repairs may
    be made without a separate correction note.
  </p>
  <p>
    We cannot promise a particular outcome when sources conflict. In that case,
    the page should explain the uncertainty and direct readers to the manual or
    authority governing their specific engine, installation or operation.
  </p>

  <h2 id="business-listings">Business listings</h2>
  <p>
    Owners and authorised representatives can request changes to business names,
    contact details, service areas or listing status. Please identify your
    relationship to the business and provide a current public source where
    possible. We may remove a listing while disputed details are checked.
    Inclusion remains informational and is not an endorsement.
  </p>
</Page>
